# Pre-push intentionally does NOT re-run the heavy gate suite.
#
# The full gate set (typecheck, lint, architecture, ownership, tests, build,
# coverage) is run ONCE in the foreground BEFORE each commit — see the
# CI-gates and incremental-commit rules. Re-running it here only duplicated
# that CPU on every push, which is wasteful on constrained machines.
#
# Verification therefore happens at/before commit time (fast staged checks in
# pre-commit + the foreground gate run) and again authoritatively in CI. This
# hook is a deliberate no-op.
exit 0
